Check A, L_A: least number of children of a formula production = 1; so every formula type has mean children >= 1 for every PCFG (per-type subcriticality impossible)
Check A, L_in: least number of children of a formula production = 1; so every formula type has mean children >= 1 for every PCFG (per-type subcriticality impossible)
Check B: prod_(k<1000000) (1 - 1/(k+2)^2) = 0.500000  (exact infinite product = 1/2)
Check B: simulated P(forall-chain longer than 2000) = 0.4989 over 20000 runs (prediction prod_(k<2000) = 0.5002)
Check B: every type has mean children < 1, yet bodies are infinite with probability 1/2; Q_tau then has total mass 1/2, so Lemma 1.6's conclusion fails without a uniform bound sup_k < 1.
